\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, Holy Ghost, all-quickening fire!
\par Come, and my hallowed heart inspire,
\par Sprinkled with the atoning blood;
\par Now to my soul Thyself reveal,
\par Thy mighty working let me feel,
\par And know that I am born of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Humble, and teachable, and mild,
\par O may I, as a little child,
\par My lowly Master's steps pursue!
\par Be anger to my soul unknown,
\par Hate, envy, jealousy, be gone;
\par In love create Thou all things new.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let earth no more my heart divide,
\par With Christ may I be crucified,
\par To Thee with my own soul aspire;
\par Dead to the world and all its toys,
\par Its idle pomp, and fading joys,
\par Be Thou alone my one desire.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My will be swallowed up in Thee;
\par Ligth in Thy light still may I see,
\par Beholding Thee with open face;
\par Called the full power of faith to prove,
\par Let all my hallowed heart be love,
\par And all my spotless life be praise.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

